# Task 3: Save, export and import

## Goal
Nothing I draw is ever lost, and I can move my data between devices.

## Requirements
1. Save all templates and samples to localStorage automatically after
   every change. Load them on startup. Wrap all storage access in
   try/catch so a storage failure shows a warning instead of crashing.
2. "Export" button: downloads a JSON file named
   glyphlab-YYYY-MM-DD-HHMM.json containing everything.
3. "Import" button: loads a JSON file. Ask whether to MERGE with or
   REPLACE current data.
4. Include a `version: 1` field at the top of the saved format, so
   the format can change later without breaking old files.
5. Separately keep a log of every glyph drawn in any mode (with
   timestamp and mode), included in the export. This is my raw
   dataset for later.

## Acceptance checks
- Reloading the page keeps all my templates.
- Exporting on my iPad and importing on my laptop gives identical
  templates.
- Importing a broken or unrelated JSON file shows a clear error and
  changes nothing.
